**Phase 1-4 summary:** The critical loop writes `*p++=(char) c;` then evaluates the continue guard. The guard `((size_t) (p-command) < (MagickPathExtent-1))` is evaluated after increment, so when `p-command == MagickPathExtent-1` the condition fails, execution falls to `*p='\0'` writing at index `MagickPathExtent-1` (the last valid byte of `command[MagickPathExtent]`), then resets `p=command`. Max write index is therefore MagickPathExtent-1: in bounds. This is the patched form of the known PCL/PS delegate overflow.

Other checks: `sscanf` uses `%lf` into doubles, no `%s`; `FormatLocaleString` calls are bounded by MagickPathExtent; delegate command format string comes from trusted delegate config, not user data; `delegate_info` NULL is checked before use; `image == NULL` after ReadImage is checked; `CastDoubleToLong` guards double-to-integer conversion of bounds; page dimensions only feed a formatted geometry string, not an allocation index. `AcquireUniqueSymbolicLink` failure is checked and returns. No use-after-free: `image=DestroyImage(image)` is followed by reassignment from `ReadImage`.

No candidate survived Phase 4 verification with a concrete trigger.

