**Phase 1-4 summary:** In the FTPWHO block, when `sl >= sizeof shm_data_cur->filename`, the code copies exactly `sizeof filename` bytes into the buffer with no terminating NUL byte (the branch above sets `filename[sl]=0`, this one does not). The shared-memory `filename` is later read as a C string by ftpwho consumers, causing an out-of-bounds read/info disclosure. Also the source offset `sl - sizeof(filename) - 1U` is off by one relative to the intended "last N bytes" copy, shifting the window.

Concrete trigger: STOR with a name of length 4096 while `filename` is e.g. 256 bytes; all 256 bytes filled with non-NUL characters, string reads run past the field.

