**Phase 1-4 summary:** The ID-length comment block allocates `length+MagickPathExtent` bytes with `AcquireQuantumMemory` (uninitialized), then does `count=ReadBlob(image,tga_info.id_length,comment);` without checking `count`. A truncated file (e.g. id_length=200 with only 10 bytes remaining) leaves bytes 10..199 uninitialized; `comment[id_length]='\0'` then `SetImageProperty(...,"comment",comment)` stores/exposes heap contents in image metadata. No guard checks the short-read; the only other guards (`~length` check, NULL check) do not cover it. Concrete trigger: header followed by id_length=0xFF and EOF immediately after the header.

Other candidates (colormap index via `ConstrainColormapIndex`, `offset >= image->rows` reset, RLE runlength read check, per-pixel ReadBlob size checks) are all guarded and rejected.

