Phase 1-4 summary: In run mode, `DecodeRun(length, ...)` returns a run count; the `while(run)` loop writes `*lp++` and decrements `length` without checking `length` reaching zero. If the decoded run exceeds the remaining samples on the line (crafted bitstream), `length` underflows past 0 and writes continue beyond the line buffer. No guard in Phase 2 protects this loop (the only bounds context is the `length` argument passed to DecodeRun, whose result is not re-validated). The outer `while(++lp,--length)` also relies on length reaching exactly 0.

Concrete trigger: line width 16, decoded run value 64 → 64 writes into a 16-LONG buffer, 48 LONGs out of bounds.

