Phase analysis: `header->ordnum = f.readWord()` allows up to 65535; the loop copies `orders[i]` into `header->ord[j++]` with no bound against the fixed-size `ord[]` array (256 entries in XModule). Similarly `header->insnum`/`patnum` are unbounded words indexing fixed `instr[]`/`phead[]` arrays. No guard exists anywhere for these.

Trigger: craft an S3M with ordnum = 0x1000 (4096) and no 255 terminator, so 4096 bytes are written into a 256-byte `ord` array in the module header — out-of-bounds write.

