**Phase 1-4 (condensed):** `MagickBooleanType status;` is declared uninitialized. Many `break` paths exit the object-parser loop before any assignment to `status`: e.g. the very first iteration with `ldblk > 9999` (feed a file whose first LSB long is 0x10000), or `HDR.Type[3] != 0`, `HDR.Type[2] != 0`, `HDR.imagf` invalid. Also the `image_info->ping` path jumps to `skip_reading_current` without assigning status before it's later tested. After the loop, `if (status == MagickFalse) return(DestroyImageList(image));` reads the uninitialized value, so control flow (and destruction of the image list / returned pointer) depends on stack garbage. Concrete trigger: a 4-byte file containing `0x27 0x10 0x00 0x00` (10000) → `ldblk > 9999` → immediate `break` → `status` never written.

No effective guard covers this; every other candidate (nameLen bounded to 0xFFFF, zero-dimension checks, NULL quantum_info check, ReadBlob count check) is effective.

