Phase analysis: allocation is `attribute_count + 1 (+declared_nspaces) (+1 lang)`, but the attribute loop writes up to TWO entries per attribute (a namespace declaration plus the attribute itself), so with N attributes each having a distinct out-of-scope namespace not in declared_nspaces, writes reach 2N+1 entries into a buffer sized N+1 → heap out-of-bounds write. The duplicate-check loop is also buggy (`element->attributes[j]->nspace` instead of comparing against `nspace_declarations[j].nspace` for attribute i), making duplicate suppression unreliable. Also the xml:lang escape passes `buf_length` as the output capacity rather than remaining space after the 10-byte prefix.

Concrete trigger: element with 2 attributes in distinct namespaces `a:x="1" b:y="2"` neither in scope → alloc 3 entries; writes indices 0(elem ns),1(a ns),2(attr a),3(b ns)... index 3 is out of bounds.

