**Phase 1-4 summary:** The header check `if (tok->n_args > 1)` guarantees only `args[0]` and `args[1]` exist. On the failure branch the log prints `escaped(tok->args[2])` — an index one past what the guard validated. Concrete trigger: a document line `network-status-version 3 bogusflavor` → n_args == 2, `networkstatus_parse_flavor_name("bogusflavor")` returns -1, and `tok->args[2]` is read out of bounds (args array allocated with 2 entries in memarea), then dereferenced as a string by `escaped()`. Reachable before any signature verification, so remotely triggerable by any directory document.

Also `find_opt_by_keyword(tokens, K_LEGACY_DIR_KEY)` uses `tok->args[0]` without an n_args assertion, but the token table typically enforces GE(1); the flavor read is the definite defect.

